╰┈➤ 𝗠𝘆𝗦𝗤𝗟 Server?{ one of the most misunderstood concepts]
Students often think MySQL and MySQL Server are different products
MySQL Server is the actual database engine -> It runs as a background service
Even when no application is open, the server can still be running
Its responsibilities include:
-> Managing databases
-> Processing SQL queries
-> Managing users and passwords
-> Handling multiple client connections
-> Writing data to disk
-> Reading data from disk -> It is the heart of MySQL(Manam padukunnamanii heart function aagipodhu kadaa just like MySQL erver..)

╰┈➤ 𝗠𝘆𝗦𝗤𝗟 𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸𝗯𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗵?
Ippudu imagine the MySQL Server has no screen - soo How do you interact with it? -> That's where MySQL Workbench comes in

Workbench is simply a graphical client- it allows you to:
-> Connect to MySQL Server
-> Write SQL queries
-> Create databases
-> Design tables
-> View data
-> Manage users
-> Export and import databases

𝗠𝘆𝗦𝗤𝗟 𝗦𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗲𝗿 = Engine
𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸𝗯𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗵 = Dashboard anamata
Just as a car's dashboard lets you interact with the engine, Workbench lets you interact with the server anthee...

╰┈➤Server vs Workbench(Interviewsloo..)
𝗠𝘆𝗦𝗤𝗟 𝗦𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗲𝗿              𝗠𝘆𝗦𝗤𝗟 𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸𝗯𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗵     
 Stores data            | Displays data       
 Executes SQL           | Lets you write SQL  
 Runs in the background | Desktop application 
 Database engine        | Graphical interface 
=> If you close Workbench, your data is still inside MySQL Server

